🔹 Program 15: Payment Processing System

📌 Description

This program demonstrates run-time polymorphism using a real-world payment system.

"Payment" is an abstract base class containing a pure virtual function "pay()".

Different payment methods such as Card, UPI and Net Banking provide their own implementation of "pay()".

A common function "processPayment()" accepts a "Payment" reference and calls the appropriate payment method at run time.

🎯 Concepts Used

- 🔹 Abstract class
- 🔹 Pure virtual function
- 🔹 Inheritance
- 🔹 Run-time polymorphism
- 🔹 Base reference
- 🔹 Virtual destructor
